          "text": "ARRAY ORGANIZATION. 1 block = (2K + 128) bytes x 64 pages. 1G: 1024 blocks."
        },
        {
          "page": 44,
          "method": "real_source_excerpt",
          "text": "Status C0H includes ECCS1 ECCS0 P_FAIL E_FAIL WEL OIP. P_FAIL Program Fail indicates a program failure has occurred. E_FAIL Erase Fail indicates an erase failure has occurred. ECCS/ECCSE provide ECC status after a valid READ."
        },
        {
          "page": 48,
          "method": "real_source_excerpt",
          "text": "BAD BLOCK MANAGEMENT. The factory identifies invalid blocks using a Bad Block Mark. System software can create a bad-block table from the mark."
        },
